The size checks on the built contracts of abako-dev/contracts at 27e109e, run in the embedded provider's runtime
(pallet-contracts 51, 1 MiB of contract memory). Each PROBE line is printed by a temporary provider test that sets up one
Project through the provider, restores the stored state and calls the contracts directly; every call is rolled back except
the tasks. The tasks have 24 assignees, of which sixteen encode to 12,369 bytes. The proposals have ten milestones with the
stated number of requirements each.

